### Minor Findings
1. **Decorative spinner icon exposed to assistive tech**
   - **Location**: `DataLoader.jsx:16` (`<div className="spinner"></div>`)
   - **Element**: `.spinner`
   - **Impacted Group**: Screen reader users
   - **WCAG / APG**: [WCAG 1.1.1 Non-text Content (Level A)](https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/non-text-content.html)
   - **Confidence**: HIGH
   - **Why this matters**: While currently an empty `<div>`, if styled with pseudo-elements (`::before`/`::after`) or replaced with an SVG/font icon, it can pollute screen reader virtual buffers. It should be explicitly marked decorative.
   - **Fix**: Add `aria-hidden="true"` to `<div className="spinner"></div>`.

---

## What's Missing
- **`aria-busy` state**: When `isLoading` is true, the container lacks `aria-busy="true"` to tell assistive technology that content is updating.
- **Error state communication**: The component only models success (`!isLoading && data`). Real-world async data loaders must announce failed requests with clear guidance (`role="alert"` or polite error notification).
- **Heading hierarchy context**: `<h2>Results</h2>` is used directly; ensure an `<h1>` exists higher in the document tree to satisfy WCAG 1.3.1.

---

## Multi-Perspective Notes

| Perspective | Alarm Level | Trigger Signal |
|-------------|-------------|----------------|
| Screen reader | **HIGH** | Dynamic asynchronous DOM insertion without `aria-live`, `role="status"`, or `aria-busy` |
| Keyboard-only | **LOW** | Component is read-only non-interactive display |
| Low vision | **LOW** | Border and background colors are standard; text contrast of `#0066cc` border is ~4.5:1 against white |
| Cognitive | **MEDIUM** | Sudden silent layout shift when spinner disappears and results mount |
| Vestibular & motion | **MEDIUM** | Infinite rotation animation without `prefers-reduced-motion` |
| Auditory access | **LOW** | No audio media present |
| Environmental contrast | **LOW** | Basic border styling with adequate text contrast |

- **Screen reader user**: Misses the asynchronous state progression entirely. Navigating the page during the 2-second interval will read "Loading data...", but after 2 seconds, no notification is sent when "Results" appears.
- **Keyboard-only user**: No focusable interactive elements exist. If interactive controls are later placed inside the loaded data, focus management will need to ensure focus is not stranded.
- **Low vision user**: Standard reflow and sizing are adequate, but the visual disappearance of the spinner causes a layout jump without focus/status anchor.
- **Cognitive accessibility**: Needs error state communication and clear messaging if network latency is prolonged.

---

## Recommended Remediation

### 1. Updated Component Code (`DataLoader.jsx`)

```jsx
import React, { useState, useEffect } from 'react';

const DataLoader = () => {
  const [isLoading, setIsLoading] = useState(true);
  const [data, setData] = useState(null);

  useEffect(() => {
    const timer = setTimeout(() => {
      setData({ content: 'Loaded data' });
      setIsLoading(false);
    }, 2000);

    return () => clearTimeout(timer);
  }, []);

  return (
    <div
      className="data-container"
      aria-busy={isLoading}
    >
      {/* Live region for status updates */}
      <div role="status" aria-live="polite" className="sr-only">
        {isLoading ? 'Loading data...' : 'Data loaded successfully.'}
      </div>

      {isLoading && (
        <div className="loading-spinner" aria-hidden="true">
          <div className="spinner" />
          <p>Loading data...</p>
        </div>
      )}

      {!isLoading && data && (
        <section className="data-content" aria-labelledby="results-heading">
          <h2 id="results-heading">Results</h2>
          <p>{data.content}</p>
        </section>
      )}
    </div>
  );
};

export default DataLoader;
```

### 2. Updated CSS

```css
/* Screen-reader-only utility */
.sr-only {
  position: absolute;
  width: 1px;
  height: 1px;
  padding: 0;
  margin: -1px;
  overflow: hidden;
  clip: rect(0, 0, 0, 0);
  white-space: nowrap;
  border: 0;
}

.spinner {
  width: 30px;
  height: 30px;
  border: 4px solid #f3f3f3;
  border-top: 4px solid #0066cc;
  border-radius: 50%;
}

/* Respect user motion preferences */
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
  .spinner {
    animation: spin 1s linear infinite;
  }
}

@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .spinner {
    border-top-color: #0066cc;
    opacity: 0.8;
  }
}

@keyframes spin {
  0% { transform: rotate(0deg); }
  100% { transform: rotate(360deg); }
}
```

---

## Verdict Justification
**Verdict: REVISE**. While the visual layout works, the component does not meet WCAG 4.1.3 (Status Messages) or WCAG 2.2.2 (Pause, Stop, Hide). Applying `role="status"` / `aria-live="polite"`, `aria-busy`, and the `prefers-reduced-motion` media query will upgrade this to **ACCEPT**.
